driver  can  support the failure of component drives.  The number
of failures allowed depends on the parity level selected.  If the
driver is able to handle drive failures, and a drive  does  fail,
then  the  system is operating in "degraded mode".  In this mode,
all missing data must be reconstructed from the data  and  parity
present  on  the  other  components.  This results in much slower
data accesses, but does mean that a failure need  not  bring  the
system to a complete halt.  The RAID driver supports and enforces
